# Allowlist, not a denylist. Everything is excluded and the handful of things an installed
# extension actually needs are added back.
#
# A denylist has to name every private file to keep it out, which means it leaks what those
# files are and silently ships anything new that nobody remembered to add.
**

!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE.txt
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
!icon.png
!dist/**
!themes/**
!icons/**
